    {
      "id": "a763e715-353d-4e09-838e-c6fac7954eab",
      "name": "Rabea Massaad 20 Progressive Rock Licks  Lick 1",
      "source": "jtc",
      "url": "https://jtcguitar.com/learn?package=5664&track=1614",
      "description": "This lick is based around the C Phrygian Dominant mode (C Db E F G Ab Bb) featuring pinch harmonic bends, some legato and triplet time phrasing. A good lick to start a feature guitar solo.",
      "createdAt": "2026-06-30T07:33:22.627Z"
    },
    {
      "id": "b4d2e807-6c65-4c89-83f6-8eeeb60891e8",
      "name": "Rabea Massaad 20 Progressive Rock Licks  Lick 2",
      "source": "jtc",
      "url": "https://jtcguitar.com/learn?package=5664&track=1615",
      "description": "This lick has a Locrian sound, with odd notes from the start, but it actually uses the similar Dorian #4 scale (C D Eb F# G A Bb), the fourth mode of the harmonic minor scale. We're messing around with the rhythmic phrasing to create tension, and playing around with a mix of legato and picking patterns; this is one of my favorite licks.",
      "createdAt": "2026-06-30T07:34:19.816Z"
    },
    {
      "id": "28560a89-bbbe-46f2-bf02-5629a5fe0745",
      "name": "Rabea Massaad 20 Progressive Rock Licks  Lick 3",
      "source": "jtc",
      "url": "https://jtcguitar.com/learn?package=5664&track=1616",
      "description": "I decided to use notes from the blues scale (C Eb F F# G Bb), but the main reason it doesn't sound very bluesy is the rhythm of the lick along with the legato technique. The lick finishes with a phrase from the Dorian mode (C D Eb F G A Bb).",
      "createdAt": "2026-06-30T07:35:44.352Z"
    },
    {
      "id": "bfce8341-7550-45e3-8d7c-d2539e8f57a6",
