    },
    {
      "id": "cf857a39-4948-4075-907d-5dba9cd2edc0",
      "name": "Al Joseph Progressive Developments  King David",
      "source": "jtc",
      "url": "https://jtcguitar.com/learn?package=4781&track=4",
      "description": "The way I see Progressive Metal. More than just the sound quality, I've tried to make sure this track (along with the others) is as harmonically and rhythmically full as possible while maintaining the edge that metal music requires. I find that this approach fuels my creativity when composing lines and melodies. It also allows me to focus on consolidating my ideas while still allowing my lines to be as technical as I want them to be.\n\n\n\nFor this song I wanted to hit hard while touching on a couple of my main influences, John Petrucci and Marco Sfogli. Thus, using the F# Phrygian major (F# G A# B C# D E). For me, these guys are the models I use when it comes to songwriting for the guitar. You might be able to recognize the line i borrowed at the beginning ;-)\n\n\n\nPlease enjoy, and remember to bear these concepts in mind as you learn these solos!",
      "createdAt": "2026-07-10T09:54:30.692Z"
    },
    {
      "id": "49985584-0659-4e19-bd97-4a11c42f0e66",
      "name": "Al Joseph Technical Chops: Beginner  Lick 04",
      "source": "jtc",
      "url": "https://jtcguitar.com/learn?package=6512&track=13611",
      "createdAt": "2026-07-24T17:24:18.527Z"
    },
    {
      "id": "c102f2bf-f5af-41ca-9776-851de400b930",
      "name": "Al Joseph Technical Chops: Beginner  Lick 05",
      "source": "jtc",
      "url": "https://jtcguitar.com/learn?package=6512&track=13612",
      "createdAt": "2026-07-24T17:26:11.786Z"
    },
    {
      "id": "6efe2406-4ddf-428c-9275-0de933c9e67f",
      "name": "Al Joseph Progressive Developments  The Reflecting Pool",
      "source": "jtc",
      "url": "https://jtcguitar.com/learn?package=4781&track=6",
      "description": "For this tune I decided to dig up some of the influences that I grew up on, mainly P.O.D.\n\nI love this track, because for me it lets me hear how my alternative or hard rock influences can sound in a progressive metal outlet! This solo is definitely melody heavy but I was just so curious to see what would come out!",
      "createdAt": "2026-07-24T17:28:24.016Z"
    }
  ],
